# Alien vs Predator (1994).jag — reach sustained Alien first-person gameplay.
# BIOS off (core default). Frames are absolute from boot.
#
# Timeline (measured on develop @ 4eab779):
#   ~240-480  title art animates
#   ~720      main menu (SELECT CHARACTER)
#   ~900-1100 character select / confirm
#   ~1140-1500 briefing ("LOADING SIMULATION... PRESS FIRE")
#   ~1500+    in-game; hold d-pad for sustained motion
#   3000-6300 motion continues (see "keep-alive" below)
#
# Keep-alive: the input below runs to frame ~6300 so that runs longer than
# 3000 frames still land on a *live* scene.  Without it the last press ends
# at 3000, the player stands still, and every later frame is byte-identical
# to frame ~3050 (the renderer keeps re-blitting the same view, so the core's
# crash watchdog logs `video_stall` even though nothing is wrong).  A frozen
# frame silently invalidates any measurement that assumes motion.  Presses
# past the run length simply never fire, so a 3000-frame run is unaffected.

780:b:10
900:b:10
1020:b:10
1140:b:10
1260:b:15
1380:b:15
1500:b:15
1620:b:15
1740:b:10
1860:up:120
1980:right:120
2100:down:120
2220:left:120
2340:up:120
2460:right:120
2580:up:120
2700:left:120
2820:right:120
2940:up:60

